.nh
.TH "TEAMS" "1" "Oct 2026" "teams dev" "teams Manual"

.SH NAME
teams-channel-read - Read a channel's root messages


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBteams channel read  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Read a channel's messages. --since and --until are applied on the client:
the channel message endpoint supports only $top and $expand, and $filter is a
400 rather than a silent ignore, so the CLI pages the listing and stops at the
first thread older than the window (PLAN.md:187).


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--all\fP[=false]
	fetch every page instead of --limit

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for read

.PP
\fB--limit\fP=20
	maximum number of messages (newest first)

.PP
\fB--replies\fP[=false]
	include each thread's replies

.PP
\fB--since\fP=""
	only messages newer than this (a duration like 24h, or a timestamp)

.PP
\fB--team\fP=""
	team the channel belongs to (when the reference does not say)

.PP
\fB--until\fP=""
	only messages older than this (a duration like 24h, or a timestamp)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--jq\fP=""
	filter JSON output through a jq expression (implies --json)

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	machine-readable JSON output

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable colours (also honours NO_COLOR)

.PP
\fB--no-input\fP[=false]
	never prompt; fail fast instead

.PP
\fB--profile\fP=""
	profile to use (default: the configured default_profile)

.PP
\fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	suppress progress messages on stderr

.PP
\fB--read-only\fP[=false]
	refuse write commands

.PP
\fB--refresh\fP[=false]
	ignore cached names and resolve them again

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	verbose diagnostics on stderr (-v, -vv)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBteams-channel(1)\fP
